  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196588/assets/72c697336f9518e5be1c8b89d9244c0952a7b8f5e77f007638e6a9405d98d8fd.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            Find an expression in terms of $x$ for the measure of $∠ODC.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $m∠ODC=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${}^{∘}$",
  "worked_solution": "Since $\\overset{―}{OC}$ and $\\overset{―}{OD}$ are radii of the circle, the triangle $△OCD$ is isosceles. Consequently, the base angles must have the same measure:\n\n$$\n∠OCD=∠ODC.\n$$\n\nAlso, from step 3, we know that $m∠COD={(180-10x)}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196588/assets/509c6fd7ffabd5c4f7b71e89dd94cb29c374dd6d2d64407d65bcdef44553c60e.png)\n\nNow, since the internal angles of any triangle sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠ODC+m∠OCD+m∠COD & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠ODC+(m∠ODC)+(180-10x)^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠ODC-10{x}^{∘} & ={0}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠ODC & =10{x}^{∘} \\\\ m∠ODC & =5{x}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $m∠ODC=5{x}^{∘}.$",
